Book Writer desktop app — bundled embedding model attribution
===============================================================

This directory ships a redistributed, third-party machine-learning model
used entirely offline by the Book Writer desktop app's native semantic RAG
feature. It is not source code written by this project. It is included here,
under Apache License 2.0 Section 4(d), to travel with the redistributed
artifact.

Upstream model
  sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
  https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2

ONNX conversion actually shipped
  Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (an ONNX export/conversion of the upstream model)
  https://huggingface.co/Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2

License
  Apache License 2.0 (see the LICENSE file in this same directory), as
  declared by both the upstream model card and the Xenova ONNX-conversion
  model card.

Files redistributed by this app (see manifest.json in this directory for
exact SHA-256 digests, byte sizes, and source URLs)
  - model_quantized.onnx  (the model weights)
  - tokenizer.json
  - tokenizer_config.json
  - config.json

Notice of modification (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b))
  The redistributed model weights are NOT the original upstream fp32
  weights. Xenova converted the upstream PyTorch model to the ONNX format
  and applied 8-bit dynamic quantization ("q8") to produce
  model_quantized.onnx. Book Writer performs no further modification of the
  model weights; it downloads the exact bytes published by Xenova at the
  source URL recorded in manifest.json, verifies their SHA-256 digest before
  every load (see app/desktop/src/main/rag/modelManifest.ts), and
  repackages those verified bytes, unmodified, inside its installer.

No network access
  The app ships this model as a local, offline resource. It does not
  download the model at runtime, and nothing in the shipped app is
  configured to fetch model or tokenizer files from Hugging Face or any
  other remote host at runtime.

